# The documentation-maturity floors are ALL 0.0 — an advisory, not-yet-tier-gated
# axis: it scores and advises but every tier is reachable at any score, so it never
# caps the roll-up meet and cannot drop a slice's ratchet tier. The 0.0 floors are a
# not-yet-tier-gated POLICY, NOT score calibration (the score is the objective bounded
# coverage fraction owned by slices/core/documentation); the burn-down ratchet lives
# in the ontology-resident gmeow:AxisFloorCommitment individuals (generated/governance/slice-quality-axis-floors.tsv
# is a read-only projection of them), floored at each slice's committed score.
